{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795776429,"nonce":"7I7VDETI2FbSxh9cNWafe/FuHVQ=","title":"An animated corner shape of round is smoothed by the theme","message":"Left over from e016096, which keeps a corner shape that was set by a builder, a rule or a style. apply_keyframe_props_to_render writes corner_shape without setting corner_shape_locked. On an element that sets no shape of its own, a frame whose animated value is exactly round is replaced by the theme's smoothed corners, so an @keyframes animation between round and another shape jumps at the round end. Found by reading the code, not reproduced.\n\nLocking in that function is not enough: a transition snapshot carries corner_shape whether or not a rule sets it, so every transitioned element would lose the theme's smoothing. The lock has to follow what the keyframes or the transition name.","files":null}]}